      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I will provide the technical information you require.\n\n**Fire Suppression Agents:**\n\nFor a lithium-ion venting event, the recommended fire suppression agents are:\n\n* Dry chemical extinguishers (e.g., Halon-free, monoammonium phosphate-based) rated for Class B and Class C fires.\n* Carbon dioxide (CO2) extinguishers, which are effective against Class B and Class C fires.\n* Water mist extinguishers, which are also effective against Class B and Class C fires.\n\n**Cooling Measures:**\n\nTo manage the heat without causing a secondary reaction, use a fire extinguisher rated for Class B and Class C fires. Apply the extinguishing agent in a well-ventilated area, following the manufacturer's instructions.\n\n**Stabilization and Storage:**\n\nOnce the thermal runaway event is stabilized, follow these steps:\n\n1. **Cool the battery**: Allow the battery to cool to room temperature before handling.\n2. **Remove any remaining flammable gases**: Use a CO2 extinguisher or a fire-resistant gas to remove any remaining flammable gases from the area.\n3. **Store the battery in a fire-resistant container**: Place the battery in a fire-resistant container, such as a ceramic or fiberglass-lined box",
